+/// holder.list;`) initialises an independent one. Only initialisation that
+/// already reached the use site counts. The discriminator is always the
+/// alias's own initializer, never the target's type: `&root` shares the
+/// object, a struct copy does not.
+fn bindingDerivedFrom(
